            <ArticleTitle>Intraosseous lipoma of lamina of the first thoracic vertebra: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>E250-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="STUDY DESIGN" NlmCategory="METHODS">A case is reported.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To report a case of intraosseous lipoma involving the lamina of the first thoracic vertebra.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="SUMMARY OF BACKGROUND DATA" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">Intraosseous lipomas involving the spine rarely have been reported.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">An incidental intraosseous lesion of the lamina of the first thoracic vertebra documented on magnetic resonance imaging was surgically excised and pathologically evaluated.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">The histologic findings were consistent with those for intraosseous lipomas previously reported in other bones.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">The authors present a rare case of an intraosseous lipoma involving the lamina of the first thoracic vertebra.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
